WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.720
This briefing comes from Book 09 of
the Federal Modernization Workbook,

2
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:08.690
Network and Transport: how to
move branch traffic off the long

3
00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:12.738
hairpin without turning a latency
gain into a compliance loss.

4
00:00:12.738 --> 00:00:16.651
I'll take four questions: why
physics decides the architecture,

5
00:00:16.651 --> 00:00:20.263
what has to change, who owns the
network, and how to get there.

6
00:00:20.263 --> 00:00:23.555
The short version: no product
shortens a fiber path,

7
00:00:23.555 --> 00:00:27.220
so buy transport on physics,
and govern it as compliance.
